# Tailwind v4 canonical classes

Never introduce classes that trigger `tailwindcss(suggestCanonicalClasses)`. Prefer theme tokens and suffix important.

## Theme colors and shadows (preferred)

Admin palette is registered in `@theme inline` (`globals.css`). Use theme utilities, not CSS-var arbitrary values:

```tsx
// BAD
className="text-[var(--admin-ink)] bg-[var(--admin-paper)] border-[var(--admin-line)]"
className="text-(--admin-ink) shadow-(--admin-shadow)"

// GOOD
className="text-admin-ink bg-admin-paper border-admin-line shadow-admin"
```

Storefront already uses theme names: `text-ink`, `bg-paper`, `border-hairline`, `shadow-card`, `text-brass`.

Spacing tokens: `pt-chrome-height`, `-mt-chrome-height`, `top-chrome-height`, `pl-carousel-gap`.

If you need a new shared color/spacing/shadow, add it to `@theme inline` first, then use the utility name.

## Important modifier (suffix only)

```tsx
// BAD
className="!w-auto !h-10 sm:!px-4"

// GOOD
className="w-auto! h-10! sm:px-4!"
```

Never rewrite TypeScript `!` (negation / non-null) when fixing classes. Only edit string literals / `className` values.

## Common arbitrary → canonical maps

| Avoid | Use |
| --- | --- |
| `tracking-[0.1em]` | `tracking-widest` |
| `min-w-[640px]` | `min-w-160` |
| `z-[80]` / `z-[40]` | `z-80` / `z-40` |
| `supports-[backdrop-filter]:…` | `supports-backdrop-filter:…` |
| `text-[var(--token)]` | theme utility, or `text-(--token)` only if no theme token exists |

Keep true one-offs as arbitrary values when no theme/scale match exists (e.g. `text-[11px]`, `min-h-[17rem]`, `shadow-[0_24px_48px_…]`).

## Before finishing UI work

Scan new/edited `className` strings for `[var(--`, prefix `!utility`, and obvious scale equivalents. Do not leave Problems-panel canonical warnings behind.
